Spoiler related to going upstairs with Amulet while in Hell:

In article <1993Sep10.110753.1@vxdesy.desy.de> pawlak@vxdesy.desy.de writes:
>> Am I doomed to remain in hell or is there another way of making my
>> way up.

>And yes, the Amulet prevents you from level teleports. So you have to be
>patient and try, and try, and try... The only drop of optimism I can 
>give you is that once you manage to leave the hell you'll be able go 
>go straight up (no sucking back any more).

I found the following through playing not by reading source, thus I
have no idea why it works and/or if I just happened to find an
exploitable bug in my version [first official Amiga binary release - 3.1.3].

1. get to upstairs.
2. if wearing Amulet, take off Amulet.
3. drop Amulet.
4. go up.
5. go down.
   [ Steps 4 and 5 may not be needed, I don't recall since I last played. ]
6. pick up Amulet.
7. go up.

You never get teleported back down levels.  It makes playing much more fun.

